(3532719, 490187, 60862, '<td valign="top">This is perfect.  Seeing old things in modern times isn''t nearly as jarring as seeing modern things in old times.  So your idea easily beats the ribbon winners in my book.<br/> <br/>And then, of course, you have the typical timfythetoo image quality on top of the perfect idea. :)</td>', 'This is perfect.  Seeing old things in modern times isn''t nearly as jarring as seeing modern things in old times.  So your idea easily beats the ribbon winners in my book. And then, of course, you have the typical timfythetoo image quality on top of the perfect idea. :)', '2007-04-09 13:27:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(3532826, 490894, 60862, '<td valign="top">Hi, and welcome to DPC.<br/> <br/>I''m guessing there are two problems with this entry, both of which could result in it being disqualified: it was taken outside the challenge dates and it looks like you pasted parts of other pictures in the upper left corner.<br/> <br/>Other than in challenges with "expert" editing rules, you''re not allowed to combine more than one shot in your entry.<br/> <br/>Don''t worry too much about it - just take it as learning how DPC works and keep entering. :)</td>', 'Hi, and welcome to DPC. I''m guessing there are two problems with this entry, both of which could result in it being disqualified: it was taken outside the challenge dates and it looks like you pasted parts of other pictures in the upper left corner. Other than in challenges with "expert" editing rules, you''re not allowed to combine more than one shot in your entry. Don''t worry too much about it - just take it as learning how DPC works and keep entering. :)', '2007-04-09 14:03:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(3532830, 491548, 60862, '<td valign="top">Kashi:  "anachronism" means something that doesn''t belong in its time, as opposed to just showing something old with something new.  I think some of the highest-scoring entries don''t really show anachronism, but timfythetoo''s 4th place entry does perfectly.<br/> <br/>Now, as a picture, well, you said it yourself. :)</td>', 'Kashi:  "anachronism" means something that doesn''t belong in its time, as opposed to just showing something old with something new.  I think some of the highest-scoring entries don''t really show anachronism, but timfythetoo''s 4th place entry does perfectly. Now, as a picture, well, you said it yourself. :)', '2007-04-09 14:05:46.000000', NULL, 0),
